// The rigidcollide package: the collision half of a Jolt-like rigid-body
// physics engine. A program reaches it with 'import rigidcollide', and gets:
//
// - Shapes: sphere, box, capsule, cylinder, convex hull (quickhull from
//   points), triangle mesh (with its own BVH), heightfield, and compound (a
//   list of shapes with local transforms). Every shape answers its local
//   bounding box, mass properties (volume, centre of mass, inertia tensor at
//   unit density), a support function and a ray cast.
// - Narrow phase: GJK (distance and overlap) and EPA (penetration depth and
//   normal), fast paths for sphere-sphere, sphere-capsule, capsule-capsule and
//   box-box (SAT), and contact manifolds of up to 4 points built by clipping
//   the two supporting faces (Sutherland-Hodgman), as Jolt and Bullet do.
// - Queries: ray cast, shape cast (conservative advancement), overlap tests,
//   closest points and distance, against any shape.
// - Broad phase: pluggable. 'BroadPhase' is the interface the world uses
//   (insert, update, remove, pairs, ray and box queries); 'SweepAndPrune' is a
//   sort-and-sweep implementation of it.
//
// The solver lane builds on this: it owns bodies and the contact cache; this
// package owns geometry only and keeps no state between calls.
//
// Conventions are geomath's: right-handed, y up, metres, f32. A 'Rigid' is a
// rotation and a translation (no scale: a shape's size is in the shape).
// A manifold's normal points from shape A towards shape B; a point's depth is
// positive when the shapes overlap there and negative when they are apart
// within the speculative margin the caller asked for.
//
// Against a mesh or heightfield the manifolds follow Jolt: a contact within
// 8 degrees of its triangle's normal takes that normal, ghost contacts at flat
// edges are dropped (active edges), and the manifolds one shape makes with a
// flat patch (same parts, normals within 2 degrees) are merged into one of at
// most four points. Compounds nest: a Shape's 'parts' keep the nesting and its
// 'leaves' are the prims with composed transforms that the narrow phase walks.
//
// What it does not do (yet): rotation in a shape cast (translation only);
// one-sided triangles; a plane shape; a convex radius on hulls and boxes (Jolt
// rounds them; here a box is sharp and GJK works on the exact core); scaled
// shapes; SIMD. Clipping and manifold building use inline fixed buffers (no
// allocation); GJK/EPA, the mesh walk and the caller's output list are still
// heap Lists.
//
// Method choices (each is a published algorithm, cited where it is coded):
//   GJK                      van den Bergen / Ericson, with Jolt's core+radius split
//   EPA                      van den Bergen, "Proximity Queries and Penetration Depth"
//   box-box                  SAT over 15 axes (Gottschalk; Ericson 4.4.1), then face clip
//   box-triangle             SAT over 13 axes (Akenine-Moller 2001; Ericson 5.2.9), then clip
//   GJK sub-simplices        64-bit barycentric weights (Ericson 5.1.5 in f64): in f32 they
//                            lose the origin on triangles tens of metres across
//   EPA guard                a depth beyond the cores' widths falls back to the least overlap
//                            along candidate axes (separating axis idea)
//   mesh contacts            Jolt: face-normal snap, active edges, merge per body pair
//   manifold                 Sutherland-Hodgman clip of the incident face (Ericson; Jolt's
//                            ManifoldBetweenTwoFaces), reduced to 4 points as Jolt does
//   convex hull              quickhull (Barber, Dobkin, Huhdanpaa 1996)
//   mass properties          Eberly, "Polyhedral Mass Properties (Revisited)"
//   mesh BVH                 binned SAH build, stack traversal
//   shape cast               conservative advancement (van den Bergen; Jolt's CastShape)
//   sweep and prune          sort along the axis of greatest variance (Bullet's/ODE's way)
//
//   mathx.cone      scalar helpers, Rigid
//   shape.cone      Prim, Shape, bounds, support, mass properties
//   hull.cone       quickhull
//   bvh.cone        triangle-mesh BVH, heightfield cells
//   raycast.cone    ray casts against every shape
//   gjk.cone        GJK and EPA
//   manifold.cone   Manifold, face clipping, fast paths, collide()
//   query.cone      shape cast, overlap, closest points
//   broadphase.cone BroadPhase and SweepAndPrune

mod rigidcollide;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
